<article class="env-lemma" id="0DDG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DDG">Lemma <span data-tag="0DDG">59.92.1</span>.</a> Let $K/k$ be an extension of separably closed fields. Let $X$ be a proper scheme over $k$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a torsion abelian sheaf on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. Then the map $H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}) \to H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(X_ K, \mathcal{F}|_{X_ K})$ is an isomorphism for $q \geq 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Looking at stalks we see that this is a special case of Theorem <a href="/tag/095T" data-tag="095T">59.91.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>